{title: Sons of Hagabah}
{subtitle: Ezra 2:45; Nehemiah 7:48; Ezra 2:43–46; Nehemiah 11:21}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 79}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
From Babylon we [F]came back home
[Eb]Walking down the [F]dusty road
[Gm]Zerubbabel [F]led the way
We [Eb]carried light to break the night
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm]Sons of Le[Eb]banah and Sons [F]of Ha[Gm]gabah
Names [Eb]written in the holy book
Sons of [Bb]Ak[Gm]kub walking through
[F]Restoring what [Eb]was torn and lost
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Temple ser[Gm]vants with no name
Sons of [F]Ziha and [Eb]Hasupha
Serving [F]God in hum[Gm]ble way
Rebuild[F]ing faith that stayed with [Eb]us
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sons of Lebanah [Gm]and Sons of [Eb]Hagabah
Names [F]written [Gm]in the ho[Eb]ly book
Sons of Akkub walking [Bb]through [F/A]
[Gm]Restoring what [F]was torn and lost
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Nehemiah count[F]ed every [Gm]soul [Eb][F][Gm][Eb][F][Gm][Eb][F][Gm][Eb][F]
[Gm]Lebana and Haga[F]ba there
Shalmai [Eb]standing shoulder to [F]shoulder
Du[Gm]ties assigned [F]in ancient air
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]Lived on Ophel serving [Gm]God
Ziha and Gish[F]pa in charge
[Eb]Our names re[F]main in the [Gm]book
Forever in [F]the sacred [Eb]page
{end_of_verse}

